{"id": "two-sets-of-books", "title": "Two sets of books: City payments that the recipients’ own tax returns cannot hold", "seconds": 130.3, "voice": "elevenlabs:OtHu0lbpdNTqJVqaxDtR", "narrator": "Maven", "tempo": 1.184, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "6c5aef5e389efde9", "words": 406, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "Two records of the same money. The City’s ledger says what it paid.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.02, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["the City’s ledger", "what it paid"], "b": ["the tax return", "what it took in, spent and kept"], "kicker": "Two records of the same money"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.6, 0.66, 0.78, 1.11, 1.61, 2.12, 2.45, 2.78, 2.97, 3.12, 3.3]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "The nonprofit’s tax return, signed under penalty of perjury, says what it took in.", "t0": 4.14, "t1": 8.5, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["the City’s ledger", "what it paid"], "b": ["the tax return", "what it took in, spent and kept"], "kicker": "Two records of the same money"}, "emph": ["penalty of perjury"], "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.67, 0.93, 1.46, 1.79, 2.01, 2.39, 2.5, 3.3, 3.54, 3.67, 3.75, 4.01]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Take the San Francisco Public Health Foundation.", "t0": 8.62, "t1": 10.52, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "San Francisco Public Health Foundation", "sub": "tax year ended 30 June 2022", "chip": "$13.5 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.19, 0.34, 0.81, 1.07, 1.29]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "In one year, the City paid it 13.5 million dollars.", "t0": 10.64, "t1": 13.85, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "San Francisco Public Health Foundation", "sub": "tax year ended 30 June 2022", "chip": "$13.5 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.31, 0.64, 0.78, 0.99, 1.19, 1.32, 1.69, 2.05, 2.21, 2.63]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "What revenue did its own return report?", "t0": 13.97, "t1": 15.71, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "San Francisco Public Health Foundation", "sub": "tax year ended 30 June 2022", "chip": "$13.5 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.43, 0.58, 0.76, 0.9, 1.19]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "story[1]"], "text": "1.6 million dollars.", "t0": 15.71, "t1": 17.69, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$1.6 million", "label": "total revenue on its own tax return"}, "emph": ["1.6"], "wt": [0.04, 0.59, 0.87, 1.05, 1.35]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 18.21, "t1": 19.68, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.15, 0.26, 0.82, 0.96, 1.04]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Both can’t be right.", "t0": 19.8, "t1": 20.64, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["City paid, tax year ended 30 June 2022", "$13.5 million"], "b": ["revenue on its own return", "$1.6 million"], "kicker": "San Francisco Public Health Foundation"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.34, 0.43]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Either one record is wrong, or the money was never the foundation’s to report.", "t0": 20.76, "t1": 24.25, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["City paid, tax year ended 30 June 2022", "$13.5 million"], "b": ["revenue on its own return", "$1.6 million"], "kicker": "San Francisco Public Health Foundation"}, "emph": ["never"], "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.35, 0.63, 0.77, 1.37, 1.48, 1.56, 1.78, 1.98, 2.22, 2.32, 2.92, 3.07]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "count", "ref": ["oneLine", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "We checked 2,343 returns.", "t0": 24.46, "t1": 27.17, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "12", "label": "organizations paid more by the City in a year than their whole reported revenue", "sub": "across 2,343 tax returns of 481 organizations"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.44, 0.59, 1.05, 1.25, 1.54, 2.09]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "count", "ref": ["oneLine", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "12 organizations got more from the City in a year than their whole revenue.", "t0": 27.29, "t1": 31.08, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "12", "label": "organizations paid more by the City in a year than their whole reported revenue", "sub": "across 2,343 tax returns of 481 organizations"}, "emph": ["12 organizations"], "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 1.01, 1.24, 1.39, 1.57, 1.67, 1.91, 2.02, 2.15, 2.4, 2.6, 2.81, 3.11]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "count", "ref": ["oneLine", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "For 3, the return gives no clue.", "t0": 31.2, "t1": 33.1, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "12", "label": "organizations paid more by the City in a year than their whole reported revenue", "sub": "across 2,343 tax returns of 481 organizations"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.7, 0.8, 1.13, 1.4, 1.58]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[2]"], "text": "Five Keys Schools and Programs got 54.3 million from the City in a year.", "t0": 33.22, "t1": 37.59, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["City paid Five Keys, year ended 30 June 2025", "$54.3 million"], "b": ["government grants on its return", "$44.9 million"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.42, 0.73, 0.84, 1.31, 1.52, 2.13, 2.45, 2.74, 3.18, 3.3, 3.42, 3.71, 3.79, 3.89]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[2]", "amount"], "text": "Its return shows 44.9 million of government grants. 33 organizations show a gap like that.", "t0": 37.71, "t1": 43.84, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["City paid Five Keys, year ended 30 June 2025", "$54.3 million"], "b": ["government grants on its return", "$44.9 million"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.5, 0.77, 1.26, 1.64, 1.87, 2.39, 2.51, 2.89, 3.49, 4.49, 5.14, 5.29, 5.39, 5.62, 5.79]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "suspicious[1].why"], "text": "Then the balances. Start, plus the year’s surplus, should equal the end.", "t0": 44.06, "t1": 47.86, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "St James Infirmary", "kicker": "Balances that do not roll forward", "sub": "year ended 30 June 2024"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.2, 1.21, 1.67, 1.91, 2.0, 2.29, 2.86, 3.01, 3.19, 3.33]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "suspicious[1].why"], "text": "St James Infirmary began a year with 5.9 million,", "t0": 47.98, "t1": 51.01, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "St James Infirmary", "kicker": "Balances that do not roll forward", "sub": "year ended 30 June 2024"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.46, 0.94, 1.25, 1.34, 1.58, 1.74, 2.02, 2.32, 2.49]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "suspicious[1].why"], "text": "and made a 68,843 dollar surplus.", "t0": 51.01, "t1": 54.72, "shot": "b7x", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "68,843", "label": "dollar surplus for the year", "sub": "year ended 30 June 2024"}, "emph": ["68,843"], "wt": [0.04, 0.38, 0.61, 0.73, 1.13, 1.55, 1.86, 2.15, 2.68, 3.0]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "suspicious[1].why"], "text": "It ended with?", "t0": 54.84, "t1": 56.11, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "St James Infirmary", "kicker": "Balances that do not roll forward", "sub": "year ended 30 June 2024"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.44]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "204,560 dollars.", "t0": 56.11, "t1": 59.28, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$204,560", "label": "net assets at the end of the year", "sub": "$5.8 million with no entry"}, "emph": ["204,560"], "wt": [0.04, 0.43, 0.72, 1.0, 1.61, 1.92, 2.22, 2.62]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "suspicious[1].what"], "text": "That leaves 5.8 million with no entry: money left or arrived without being named.", "t0": 59.8, "t1": 65.07, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "money has left or arrived without being named"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.46, 0.73, 1.05, 1.27, 1.66, 1.89, 2.09, 2.94, 3.19, 3.58, 3.77, 4.16, 4.45, 4.8]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "suspicious[2].why"], "text": "And one return’s closing figures should open the next.", "t0": 65.19, "t1": 67.87, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Brilliant Corners", "sub": "year ended 30 June 2022", "chip": "$263.5 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.31, 0.77, 1.13, 1.65, 1.92, 2.1, 2.24]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "suspicious[2].why"], "text": "For Brilliant Corners, the two disagree by 263.5 million dollars.", "t0": 67.99, "t1": 72.98, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Brilliant Corners", "sub": "year ended 30 June 2022", "chip": "$263.5 million"}, "emph": ["263.5 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.44, 1.01, 1.09, 1.25, 1.78, 1.94, 2.17, 2.48, 3.08, 3.48, 3.77, 4.36]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].what"], "text": "Next, one firm, Resilient Strategies LLC,", "t0": 73.2, "t1": 76.46, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "Chinese Progressive Association", "sub": "City-funded nonprofit"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Resilient Strategies LLC", "sub": "100% of a year’s spending, $18.3 million"}, {"art": "question", "name": "Not in the City’s ledger", "sub": "the firm is the real recipient"}], "kicker": "One contractor"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.55, 0.77, 1.22, 1.7, 2.42]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].what"], "text": "took 100 percent of a year’s spending at Chinese Progressive Association.", "t0": 76.46, "t1": 80.38, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "Chinese Progressive Association", "sub": "City-funded nonprofit"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Resilient Strategies LLC", "sub": "100% of a year’s spending, $18.3 million"}, {"art": "question", "name": "Not in the City’s ledger", "sub": "the firm is the real recipient"}], "kicker": "One contractor"}, "emph": ["100 percent"], "wt": [0.04, 0.25, 0.44, 0.73, 1.15, 1.35, 1.45, 1.73, 2.07, 2.21, 2.61, 3.11]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].what"], "text": "18.3 million dollars.", "t0": 80.5, "t1": 82.65, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "Chinese Progressive Association", "sub": "City-funded nonprofit"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Resilient Strategies LLC", "sub": "100% of a year’s spending, $18.3 million"}, {"art": "question", "name": "Not in the City’s ledger", "sub": "the firm is the real recipient"}], "kicker": "One contractor"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.45, 0.82, 1.05, 1.53]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "So the firm is the real recipient, and it isn’t in the City’s ledger.", "t0": 82.77, "t1": 85.75, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "Chinese Progressive Association", "sub": "City-funded nonprofit"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Resilient Strategies LLC", "sub": "100% of a year’s spending, $18.3 million"}, {"art": "question", "name": "Not in the City’s ledger", "sub": "the firm is the real recipient"}], "kicker": "One contractor"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.32, 0.59, 0.69, 0.78, 1.0, 1.64, 1.73, 1.88, 2.12, 2.2, 2.34, 2.61]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "Nothing shows the two are connected.", "t0": 85.87, "t1": 87.47, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "Chinese Progressive Association", "sub": "City-funded nonprofit"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Resilient Strategies LLC", "sub": "100% of a year’s spending, $18.3 million"}, {"art": "question", "name": "Not in the City’s ledger", "sub": "the firm is the real recipient"}], "kicker": "One contractor"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.3, 0.6, 0.7, 0.89, 1.03]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "suspicious[4].what"], "text": "Last, The Gubbio Project got 1.4 million dollars in fiscal 2025.", "t0": 87.69, "t1": 91.97, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "The Gubbio Project", "kicker": "Paid, with no return on file", "sub": "fiscal 2025", "chip": "$1.4 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.38, 0.46, 0.82, 1.22, 1.42, 1.64, 2.01, 2.17, 2.56, 2.9, 3.04, 3.37, 3.62]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "suspicious[4].what"], "text": "No return is on file yet; its last two came more than two years after year-end.", "t0": 92.09, "t1": 96.43, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "The Gubbio Project", "kicker": "Paid, with no return on file", "sub": "fiscal 2025", "chip": "$1.4 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.52, 0.65, 0.81, 1.15, 1.81, 2.01, 2.26, 2.42, 2.65, 2.74, 2.94, 3.11, 3.49, 3.76]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[5]", "suspicious[4].what"], "text": "City monitors flagged it in 2025.", "t0": 96.55, "t1": 98.64, "shot": "b13x", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "“Federal 990 return filed for most recent tax year”: Not Yet In Conformance"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.69, 0.95, 1.02, 1.1, 1.31]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "slam", "ref": ["suspicious[4].why", "suspicious[4].what"], "text": "A year with City money and no return is a year nobody can check.", "t0": 98.76, "t1": 102.01, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "slam", "words": ["577", "days", "late"], "sub": "Bindlestiff Studio’s return for the year ended 31 December 2023"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.3, 0.46, 0.73, 1.03, 1.15, 1.35, 1.8, 1.93, 2.01, 2.28, 2.64, 2.89]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "slam", "ref": ["suspicious[4].why", "suspicious[4].what"], "text": "Bindlestiff Studio filed 577 days past its extended deadline.", "t0": 102.13, "t1": 106.78, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "slam", "words": ["577", "days", "late"], "sub": "Bindlestiff Studio’s return for the year ended 31 December 2023"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.45, 0.87, 1.26, 1.5, 1.74, 2.58, 3.04, 3.4, 3.55, 4.03]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "status"], "text": "No gap here is shown to be money taken.", "t0": 107.0, "t1": 108.82, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any gap is money taken", "Which record is wrong where they disagree"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.37, 0.63, 0.76, 0.95, 1.04, 1.16, 1.4]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["innocent[0]"], "text": "Timing, pass-through money and preparer error explain many.", "t0": 108.94, "t1": 111.96, "shot": "b15a", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "What explains many gaps", "sub": "timing, pass-through money, preparer error"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.59, 1.0, 1.26, 1.41, 1.88, 2.16, 2.63]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["notEstablished[1]"], "text": "The City figure leaves out loans and district money it hands over.", "t0": 112.08, "t1": 115.19, "shot": "b15b", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "The City figure", "sub": "leaves out loans and district money it hands over"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.38, 0.78, 1.1, 1.26, 1.57, 1.71, 2.05, 2.26, 2.39, 2.67]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[8]", "established[1]"], "text": "One more test, adding the federal money each audit reports, came out mostly clean.", "t0": 115.31, "t1": 119.77, "shot": "b15c", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "A second payer added as a check", "sub": "11 of 542 return-years exceed the return"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.42, 1.05, 1.3, 1.39, 1.67, 1.93, 2.13, 2.36, 3.22, 3.43, 3.64, 4.04]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? Each organization’s audited statements. And whether the money was only passing through.", "t0": 119.89, "t1": 125.0, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Each organization’s audited financial statements for the year"}, {"who": "", "what": "Whether the payment was pass-through money held for others"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.27, 0.57, 0.89, 1.42, 2.11, 2.5, 3.09, 3.37, 3.58, 3.71, 3.91, 4.07, 4.34, 4.73]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "No authority has reviewed these gaps.", "t0": 125.12, "t1": 126.79, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.56, 0.75, 1.07, 1.27]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 126.91, "t1": 129.41, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.37, 0.49, 0.58, 1.4, 1.65, 1.8]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "found": "Two records, one gap", "lead1": "Lead 1 · balances", "lead2": "Lead 2 · one contractor", "lead3": "Lead 3 · no return", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "newsroom", "hook": "contrast"}